================================================================================================
TERM ORDERING — is V3's linear depth a scheduling artefact?
================================================================================================
  Same operator, same Trotter settings, terms regrouped into layers of
  mutually disjoint support. Depth is the critical path, so a schedule the
  transpiler can parallelise should collapse it.

     N    T  layers  depth chain  depth sorted  speedup  cx chain  cx sorted  unitary err
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     4    9       6          357           225      1.6       130        124     0.00e+00
     6   15       6          621           225      2.8       226        206     0.00e+00
     8   21       6          885           225      3.9       322        288     0.00e+00
    10   27       6         1149           225      5.1       418        370          nan
    12   33       6         1413           225      6.3       514        452          nan

  depth growth   chain order N^1.25     layer-sorted N^0.00

  A sorted exponent near 0 confirms the diagnosis: the depth was never the
  physics, it was the term ORDER, and the fix costs nothing and holds for
  every N. cx is unchanged by construction, so this is a MONEY fix only -
  V3's fidelity problem is the gate count and is untouched.

  unitary err is the spectral distance between the two product formulas.
  Reordering within a Trotter step changes the error CONSTANT, not the
  order, so a small nonzero value is expected and correct - it is the same
  approximation, not the same circuit.
